Features:

-Transfer learning with EfficientNetV2B0 (ImageNet pretrained)
-Custom classification head for binary prediction
-End-to-end dataset pipeline:
-Kaggle download
-Merging datasets
-Custom train/val/test split
-Class imbalance handling using class weights
-Threshold optimization using precision-recall curve
-Evaluation using classification metrics (precision, recall, F1-score)

Problems and Solutions:

-Class Imbalance Handling:
Dataset imbalance was addressed using:

"compute_class_weight('balanced', ...)"

Class weights are passed into training:

"model.fit(..., class_weight=class_weight_dict)"

This helps reduce bias toward the majority class.

-Threshold Optimization

Instead of using the default threshold (0.5), the model uses a data-driven threshold:

"precision, recall, thresholds = precision_recall_curve(...)"

The selected threshold minimizes the difference between precision and recall:

"optimal_idx = np.argmin(np.abs(precision - recall))"

This improves balance between:
False positives
False negatives

-Training Pipeline

Training includes:

Early stopping:
Monitors validation loss
Restores best weights

Model checkpointing:
Saves best-performing model
EarlyStopping(...)
ModelCheckpoint(...)

-Mismatched Prediction Lengths

Issue:
Predictions did not match dataset size

Fix:
"model.predict(dataset, steps=len(dataset))"

-Incorrect Prediction Shape

Issue:
Predictions had shape (N,1) instead of (N,)

Fix:
"predictions.ravel()"

-Broken Validation Split

Issue:
Validation set contained extremely few samples

Cause:
Mixing manual splitting with validation_split

Fix:
Rebuilt dataset pipeline using only manual splitting

-Class Distribution Issues

Issue:
Model biased toward majority class

Fix:
Applied class weights
Used precision/recall-based evaluation

-TensorFlow Dataset Handling Issues

Issue:
Difficulty extracting labels and counts from batched datasets

Fix:
Implemented safe label extraction and counting functions

-TensorFlow Shape Errors in Augmentation (Resolved During Development)

Issue:
Shape mismatch errors when applying per-sample augmentation

Cause:
Incorrect handling of batched tensors

Resolution:
Identified need for batch-safe operations when working with tf.data.Dataset
(Note: augmentation pipeline is defined but not currently integrated into training)
